." SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt LUA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm lua
.Nd HalfBSD userland Lua interpreter
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl EivW
.Op Fl e Ar statement
.Op Fl l Ar module
.Op Ar script Op Ar arguments ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs Lua 5.4 programs using the same upstream source as the boot loader.
All ordinary Lua standard libraries are available.
The native modules
.Sy proc , halfbsd.event , halfbsd.os ,
and
.Sy halfbsd.log
provide explicit process, kqueue, operating system and logging interfaces.
No service is started by installing this interpreter.
.Pp
.Fl e
executes a statement;
.Fl l
loads a module;
.Fl i
enters interactive mode;
.Fl v
prints the version;
.Fl E
ignores environment variables;
.Fl W
turns warnings on.
A script named
.Sq -
is read from standard input.
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
Lua scripts have the caller's privileges.
This interpreter is not a sandbox.
Privileged orchestration should use direct argument arrays through
.Sy proc
and avoid the standard library's shell-based
.Sy os.execute
and
.Sy io.popen .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr flua 1 ,
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr pdfork 2
